      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I've had this problem alot. I've actually gone as far as running tcpdump on my computer while sending the request. \n\nWith VRChat debug logging enabled (--enable-sdk-log-levels --enable-debug-gui -log), I can observe an outgoing HTTP POST, but I don't consistently see a corresponding HTTP response status.\n\nDuring troubleshooting, I captured traffic using Wireshark on my Windows 11 PC. The capture showed numerous TCP RST/ACK packets involving HTTPS connections. \n\nSo I saw, in the debug console, the request would go out, but the response returning would be inconsistent, and much of the time the TCP connection would be immediately RST/ack'ed",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
